## Agent obligations

1. Treat this inventory as the **only** required-tools source for this center.
2. Branch by **`kind`**. For `sedea-extension`, use the Sedea CLI probe/install
   contract above; never use another editor's extension profile. For `cli`,
   probe in order: (a) any **user-supplied path/command** from the install mission
   gate; (b) `command -v` / PATH on **`cli`**; (c) if PATH misses, check the
   resolved OS install path for incomplete-install detection only. Do not invent
   alternate install directories. Do not PATH-prepend SDK `bin/` as normal policy.
3. Compare discovered binary or extension version to **`minVersion`** — classify
   **missing**, **outdated** (below `minVersion`), or candidate **ok**. When
   candidate **ok** and **`latestVersionProbe`** is defined, run it — latest &gt;
   installed → **upgrade-available**; otherwise **ok**. Incomplete CLI resolution
   counts as **missing**.
4. Install or **upgrade** only after structured-choice consent (**install** or
   **upgrade**, not method/path choice). Use the **sole** listed OS method id.
   For `cli`, place the binary exactly at the OS install path and follow method
   notes and **`installUrl`** (including Unix **`gcloud`** `~/bin` symlinks). For
   `sedea-extension`, install/upgrade through the resolved Sedea CLI with
   `--force` without bundling. **Forbidden:** method pickers; install-directory
   questions; inventing latest-version sources not listed as **`latestVersionProbe`**.
5. After install, upgrade, or path override, run **every** **`dryRuns`** row in order
   with bare **`cli`** for `cli` tools or the resolved Sedea CLI for
   `sedea-extension` tools, then record pass/fail.
6. For Drive **`lsf`** / **bisync**, apply **Drive auth invoke** — SA flags and
   probe order — before suggesting **`rclone config reconnect`**.

